Ludlow, played by Josh Gad.

9
00:43:21,818 --> 00:43:27,818
Matty, played by Matt Lintz.

10
00:48:10,909 --> 00:48:16,909
Pixels (marketed as Pixels: The Movie) is a 2015 science fiction action comedy film
directed by Chris Columbus, and written by Tim Herlihy and Tim Dowling.

11
00:52:59,999 --> 00:53:05,999
Loosely adapted from the 2010 short film, it stars Adam Sandler, Kevin James,
Michelle Monaghan, Peter Dinklage, Josh Gad and Brian Cox.

12
00:57:49,090 --> 00:57:55,090
In the film, an alien force misinterprets video feeds of classic arcade games as a declaration of war,
resulting in them attacking Earth with technological recreations of icons from the games.

13
01:02:38,181 --> 01:02:44,181
The president of the United States promptly assembles a team of
former arcade champions to lead the planet's defense.

14
01:07:27,272 --> 01:07:33,272
Development began in 2010, when Sandler obtained the rights to Patrick Jean's short film via his
Happy Madison Productions company and began developing the script with Herlihy.

15
01:12:16,363 --> 01:12:22,363
In 2013, Columbus entered talks to direct the film, drawn to the nostalgic homage to 1980s arcade games such
as Pac-Man, Donkey Kong and Space Invaders, all of which were licensed for use in the film.

16
01:17:05,454 --> 01:17:11,454
Filming took place in Toronto for three months, which
involved extensive night shoots and practical sets.

17
01:21:54,545 --> 01:22:00,545
Post-production, led by Digital Domain and Sony Pictures Imageworks, focused on creating
voxelized 3D versions of arcade characters to integrate into the live-action scenes.

18
01:26:43,636 --> 01:26:49,636
Pixels was released theatrically in the United States on
July 24, 2015, by Sony Pictures Releasing.

19
01:31:32,727 --> 01:31:38,727
The film received negative reviews from critics, and grossed $245 million.

20
01:36:21,818 --> 01:36:27,818
The film explores themes of new york city, london, england,
usa president, washington dc, usa, video game.

21
01:41:10,909 --> 01:41:16,909
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
